early in the morning Israeli forces  arrive at a refugee camp in Janine  a bulldozer leads the way  Israeli Army troops fire an anti-tank  weapon a tactic called the pressure  cooker designed to get people inside the  building to flee leaving this home in  Flames then begins an hours-long armed  confrontation that leaves dozens wounded  some dead this mobile phone video  appears to capture the moment one gunman  is killed  at a nursery nearby the sound of gunfire  sends children scrambling the target of  the raid was the home of relatives of  Rod qasim a gunman who killed three  Israelis and injured several more in  April in a bar in Tel Aviv he eluded  Israeli forces for hours before they  finally fatally shot him this video  shows Israeli forces drilling holes for  explosives in his home in September then  demolishing it with a blast the Israeli  Army says on Wednesday it was looking  for two gunmen suspected of carrying out  recent shooting attacks one of them was  qasim's brother Abdul Rahman  farihazam has now lost a second son Rod  cosm's brother Abbott died in the attack  on Wednesday  they demolished our house but those are  only bricks they are not going to  destroy our determination they killed my  sons but they are not dead they are  alive in heaven we believe in God and  accept his will the raid follows an  increase in armed Palestinian attacks on  Israeli Targets in the occupied West  Bank especially in the northern cities  of Janine and Nobles the Palestinian  Authority condemned the rape with prime  minister Muhammad shtaya saying  Palestinian blood has become a ticket in  the upcoming Israeli elections some  Israeli leaders say the Palestinian  Authority appears to be losing control  on the West Bank Palestinian leaders say  the rise in attacks on Israeli forces is  due to frustration over the lack of a  peace process the Oslo Accords that  promised Palestinians their own State  nearly 30 years ago never created one  and the generation that's grown up since  then is growing in patient  hours after the attack the funerals were  underway as is required under Islamic  tradition but they are only likely to  increase Rising tensions on the West  Bank John hendron Al Jazeera romala
 

